/*
  AvroBaseline.rc - the embedded ANSI baseline container.

  ANSI_BASELINE carries one shipped .AvroEnco container (the installer default,
  "Ansi V1") as raw bytes. It is linked into Avro Keyboard.exe through
  {$R ../Layout/AvroBaseline.res} in uAvroBaseline.pas, exactly like
  Internal_Layout.res / Internal_Skin.res are linked by their loader units.

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  ---------------
  With an empty AnsiMapping\ folder the application falls back to Unicode and
  never to a compiled-in mapping (uForm1.pas, uAvroLayoutUI.pas). This resource
  is the lowest-priority versioned fallback that guarantees a fresh, wiped or
  portable install still types ANSI on first run.

  The payload is an AvroShield v3 container - ciphertext - so embedding it in
  the executable leaks no plaintext mapping. It is loaded in memory only
  (never written to disk) via AvroShieldLoadForRuntime.

  Compile from this folder with:
    brcc32 -fo"AvroBaseline.res" "AvroBaseline.rc"

  The path is relative to the compiler's working directory (this folder).
*/

ANSI_BASELINE RCDATA "..\..\assets\Ansi V1.AvroEnco"
